  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The CBN. The ministry runs fiscal policy, the bureau publishes statistics, and the commission regulates the capital market.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The National Bureau of Statistics compiles and publishes the national accounts and the consumer price index.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The FIRS. The CBN manages money, the SEC regulates securities, and the FRC monitors the budget.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The NDIC, which pays depositors up to an insured limit when a bank fails — the mechanism that stops a bank failure becoming a savings collapse.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Regulating securities, the exchange and the registration of market operators. Currency is the CBN's, customs is the customs service's, and statistics are the NBS's.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The Ministry of Finance, working with the legislature on the budget. The CBN runs monetary policy.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The MPR. The cash reserve ratio and the liquidity ratio are separate instruments, and the exchange rate is the price of the naira in another currency.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Crude oil and gas dominate export earnings, even though agriculture employs far more people — the distinction the paper repeatedly tests.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Agriculture remains the largest employer. Oil is the foreign-exchange earner but employs comparatively few people directly.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    A mixed economy: markets allocate most resources, but the state owns oil revenues, regulates prices of some products and provides infrastructure.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Derivation, which is why oil-producing states receive an additional allocation from the Federation Account.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The Federation Account, from which the monthly distribution is made under the constitutionally defined formula.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Federal, state and local government. The second is the separation of powers, the third is a sectoral classification, and the fourth is a classification of production.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The price is set in a world market the country cannot influence, so a fall cuts revenue, foreign exchange and imports at the same time.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The cost of a representative basket, whose percentage change is the inflation rate. Output is GDP, employment is a labour-market figure, and the external value of the currency is the exchange rate.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The general price level is 12 per cent higher than a year before — a comparison over twelve months, not a single month's change.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    To cover imports and support the currency. A reserve cover of less than about three months of imports is the conventional warning line.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Dearer credit reduces borrowing, investment and consumption, which restrains demand-pull inflation.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It escapes registration, taxation and statistical surveys, so official figures understate both output and employment.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It is owed in foreign currency, so repayment requires foreign exchange and a depreciation raises its naira value.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Power supply and imported raw materials raise costs, so domestic goods struggle against imports — a supply-side constraint rather than a demand one.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The Fiscal Responsibility Commission, which watches the budget and the debt rule rather than money or markets.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Devaluation, privatisation, liberalisation and fiscal discipline were the standard conditions attached to adjustment lending.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Activity outside the tax net means the formal sector carries a heavier burden, which is a standard argument for widening the tax base.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Company income tax is a federal tax. Market tolls and local rates belong to local government, and school fees are not a government revenue head at all.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    OPEC, and has been since 1971. The other three are groupings on other continents.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It is a price — the price of one currency in terms of another — and it moves with supply and demand unless it is fixed.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Exports cheaper in foreign currency, imports dearer in naira. Reversing the two is the classic error.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Oil earns the bulk of foreign exchange and a large share of government revenue while employing comparatively few people directly.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    All three components are weak relative to the income level, which is why the index sits below what GDP alone would suggest.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    A tax is a fiscal instrument. The MPR, the reserve ratio and open market operations are all monetary.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It creates new money rather than transferring existing savings, so the money supply rises and prices follow.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Diversification widens the revenue and export base so that a fall in oil prices does not translate directly into a fiscal and balance of payments crisis.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    All external transactions, of which trade in goods is only one part — services, income, transfers and capital flows are the rest.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The CBN manages the reserves as part of its monetary and exchange-rate responsibilities.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Refining at home substitutes for imported petroleum products, which are among the largest single import items.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Powers and responsibilities are divided, with most revenue collected federally and shared through the Federation Account.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Only those actively seeking work are counted, and the underemployed are counted as employed, so the headline rate misses both groups.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The FIRS collects federal taxes. The other three pair each body with another body's job.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It has too small a share of the market to influence the price, so its earnings move with a price set by others.
  ]

]

